Package: evalpheno
Type: Package
Title: Modular Phenology Models and Calibration
Version: 0.0.3.2
Encoding: UTF-8
License: GPL (>= 3)
Authors@R: 
    c(
    person(given = "Lars",
             family = "Caspersen",
             role = c("aut", "cre"),
             email = "larscaspersen42@gmail.com",
             comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0000-3057-7327")))
Maintainer: Lars Caspersen <larscaspersen42@gmail.com>
BugReports: https://github.com/larscaspersen/eval_phenoflex/issues
Description: Construct, calibrate and run temperature-driven phenology
    models for temperate trees, including 
    sequential (Ashcroft et al. (1977) <doi:10.21273/HORTSCI.12.4.347>),
    parallel (Hänninen and Kramer (2007) <doi:10.14214/sf.313>), 
    PhenoFlex (Luedeling et al. (2021) <doi:10.1016/j.agrformet.2021.108491>)
    and partial overlap (Pope et al. (2014) <doi:10.1016/j.agrformet.2014.07.009>)
    structures. Combine chill and heat accumulation
    submodels with alternative model structures. Simulate variation among
    individual buds using population models, including budbreak timing
    and the proportion of buds breaking under artificial forcing
    conditions. Calibrate the Dynamic Model 
    (Erez et al. (1990) <doi:10.17660/ActaHortic.1990.276.18>) of chill accumulation using
    interpretable characteristic parameters as suggested by 
    Egea et al. (2021) <doi:10.1093/treephys/tpaa054> and implemented for PhenoFlex by
    Caspersen et al. (2024) <doi:10.17660/ActaHortic.2024.1406.64>. Additional tools support
    cross-validation and weighted ensemble predictions
    (Caspersen et al. (2025) <doi:10.1016/j.agrformet.2025.110859>), 
    modelling successive phenological stages (Caspersen et al. (2025) <doi:10.1016/j.agrformet.2025.110824>), and joint calibration across cultivars with
    shared chill and heat accumulation submodels and cultivar-specific
    requirements (Caspersen et al. (2026) <doi:10.1007/s00484-025-03068-2>).
